From f5d24c193d5bee53af37eb80bc5c405b3d6622bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:56:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 32/53] drm/gma500: submit sgxfive transfer jobs from userspace

Add DRM_IOCTL_SGXFIVE_SUBMIT_JOBS. A call is validated as a whole before
anything is queued: each job's context, flags and transfer command, its
sync operations and that every syncobj it signals exists. Then each job
is armed on its context's entity in order, waits on its syncobj
dependencies and signals its syncobjs, binary or timeline, with the
scheduler's finished fence. On an error the job count reports the job
that failed. Set DRIVER_SYNCOBJ and DRIVER_SYNCOBJ_TIMELINE so userspace
can create the syncobjs.

Assisted-by: LLM
